          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.165,
            0.579,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this chapter, you have studied the following points :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.193,
            0.835,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The distance between "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { P } ( \\boldsymbol { x } _ { 1 } , \\boldsymbol { y } _ { 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { Q } ( x _ { 2 } ,   y _ { 2 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt{ \\left( x_{2} - x_{1} \\right)^{2} + \\left( y_{2} - y_{1} \\right)^{2} }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.222,
            0.709,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The distance of a point "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { P } ( x , y )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from the origin is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt { x ^ { 2 } + y ^ { 2 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.246,
            0.901,
            0.291
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The coordinates of the point "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { P } ( x , y )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which divides the line segment joining the points "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A } ( \\boldsymbol { x } _ { \\mathrm { 1 } } , \\boldsymbol { y } _ { \\mathrm { 1 } } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { B } ( x _ { _ 2 } , y _ { _ 2 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " internally in the ratio "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m _ { \\mathrm { ~ l ~ } } : m _ { \\mathrm { ~ 2 ~ } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.293,
            0.426,
            0.336
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{m_{1}x_{2} + m_{2}x_{1}}{m_{1} + m_{2}}, \\frac{m_{1}y_{2} + m_{2}y_{1}}{m_{1} + m_{2}} \\right)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.338,
            0.898,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The mid-point of the line segment joining the points "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { P } ( \\boldsymbol { x } _ { 1 } , \\boldsymbol { y } _ { 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb{Q}(x_{2},y_{2})"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( \\frac{x_{1} + x_{2}}{2}, \\frac{y_{1} + y_{2}}{2} \\right)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.372,
            0.432,
            0.623,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A NOTETOTHE READER"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.468,
            0.855,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Section 7.3 discusses the Section Formula for the coordinates "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(x,y)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of a point P which divides internally the line segment joining the points "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A } ( \\boldsymbol { x } _ { 1 } , \\boldsymbol { y } _ { 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{B}(x_{_2},y_{_2})"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in the ratio "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m_{_1} : m_{_2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as follows :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.544,
            0.671,
            0.588
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "x = \\frac{m_{1}x_{2} + m_{2}x_{1}}{m_{1} + m_{2}} , \\quad y = \\frac{m_{1}y_{2} + m_{2}y_{1}}{m_{1} + m_{2}}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.601,
            0.497,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that, here, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{PA} \\bar{\\bar{}} : \\mathrm{PB} = m_1 : m_2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.628,
            0.855,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "However, if P does not lie between A and B but lies on the line AB, outside the line segment AB, and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{PA}:\\mathrm{PB}=m_{1}:m_{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " we say that P divides externally the line segment joining the points A and B. You will study Section Formula for such case in higher classes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
